slos.description:
apply properties/ laws of union and intersection to solve, problems using Venn diagram of:
a. two distinct and overlapping sets,
b. three overlapping sets;

write composite functions in the form of:
a. g(f(x)) or (g ∘ f)(x),
b. f(g(x)) or (f ∘ g)(x);

apply factor theorem to:
a. factorise a cubic polynomial,
b. find zeros of a polynomial;

calculate square root of algebraic expressions by:
a. factorisation,
b. division;

convert an algebraic fraction into partial fractions when its denominator consists of:
a. non-repeated linear factors,
b. repeated linear factors;

determine the gradient of a straight line:
a. when coordinates of two points are given,
b. when inclination is given;

determine the gradient of:
a. parallel lines,
b. perpendicular lines;

describe equation of a straight line in:
a. slope-intercept form,
b. point-slope form;
